  "problem_description": "Perform dimensional analysis for compressible wall-bounded channel turbulence to derive the dimensionless form of the normalized mean velocity (denoted as u+). \nThis analysis uses ONLY the following 6 physical quantities as input parameters: \nthe wall-normal distance (y), the wall density (ρ_w), the wall dynamic viscosity (μ_w), the fluid density (ρ), the dynamic viscosity (μ), and the friction velocity (u_tau). \nTo ensure comparability with the log-law and uniqueness of results, the power of wall units must be constrained to 1 for the INPUT and 0 for the OUTPUT formula.",
